      <section class="ui-section-about">
        <div class="ui-layout-container">
          <p class="ui-text-intro">Google Search Console is Google’s free service for site owners. It shows how Google Search sees a website: which pages are indexed, which queries they appear for and how often people click through to them. For most teams it is the only first-party source of data on how their site performs in Google’s organic results.</p>
          <p class="ui-text-intro">Its Performance report is the core of the tool. It records four metrics, clicks, impressions, click-through rate and average position, and breaks them down by query, page, country, device and search appearance.</p>
          <p class="ui-text-intro">Beyond performance, Search Console reports on page indexing, sitemaps, Core Web Vitals, HTTPS and structured data, and alerts site owners when Google finds a problem that could keep pages out of the results.</p>
          <p class="ui-text-intro">It keeps up to 16 months of search data, and a property can cover a whole domain, with every subdomain and protocol, or a single URL prefix. The service is free to use and connects with Google Analytics 4, so search queries can be read alongside what visitors do once they land.</p>
          <!-- CTA -->
          <div class="ui-component-cta ui-layout-flex">
            <a href="https://search.google.com/search-console/about?utm_source=webperfreport&utm_medium=website&utm_campaign=about" rel="noopener" target="_blank" role="link" aria-label="Explore Google Search Console" class="ui-component-button ui-component-button-normal">Explore Google Search Console</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
